      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0070",
      "source_en": "Lesson 30. Minor Scale Key Signatures\n\nMinor keys use the key signature of their relative major, and introduce accidentals as needed for the harmonic and melodic minor forms.\n\nE b Major C Minor: Natural Harmonic Melodic\n\nPractice\n\n1. Write the key signature for each of these minor keys. Hint: First identify the relative major for each of these minor scales.\n\nE Minor G Minor D Minor B Minor F# Minor F Minor",
